# 7. KHAYA AI — AFRICAN LANGUAGE ACCESSIBILITY

Integrate Khaya AI / GhanaNLP as a language-accessibility layer.

Its purpose is to make Farmova understandable and usable by Ghanaian farmers.

Prioritise:

- Twi.
- English.
- Other supported Ghanaian languages as verified.

The farmer should be able to interact through speech where supported.

### Desired interaction

Farmer:

"Me pɛ sɛ meyɛ adwuma wɔ me afuw no mu."

Farmova should understand the farmer's request where the configured language services support it and respond in understandable Twi.

### Implementation requirements

- Investigate the actual Khaya API documentation.
- Verify available translation, speech recognition and speech synthesis endpoints.
- Do not assume all three capabilities exist.
- Integrate only documented capabilities.
- Keep API credentials on the server.
- Implement a provider abstraction so another supported speech provider can be added if required.
- Allow text interaction when voice is unavailable.
- Include clear microphone controls.
- Allow the farmer to replay spoken responses.
- Ask one question at a time.
- Confirm important answers.
- Allow corrections.
- Provide picture-based alternatives when voice recognition fails.

Use natural, respectful language.

Do not produce awkward machine-translated farming instructions.

Have Twi content reviewed by a competent native speaker before presenting it as final.

